WEBVTT

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.740
Batting second: right fielder, Sakakibara-kun.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.440
<i>My serious fastballs don't work...</i>

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.660
<i>I don't have any way to strike this guy out for sure.</i>

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.680
A-All right!

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.640
A-All right!

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.600
Out! Game over!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.560
We did it!

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.560
Shigeno!

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.990
<i>Nice game.</i>

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.080
<i>However...</i>

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.080
<i>we might have paid too high a price for this victory.</i>

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.470
Really!

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:33.000
I told you that it would take three months to return to normal.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.890
It's caused an infection and is swollen, but it hasn't gotten worse.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.120
The swelling should go down in about two or three days.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.360
However...

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.050
if you continue to push yourself,

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.120
I won't be able to guarantee your future as an athlete!

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.740
Do you understand? This is the last time!

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.920
If you do it one more time-

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.790
And?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.520
The next game...

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.750
how many pitches will I be able to throw?

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.990
D-Don't fool around!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.400
If you can't listen to my warnings,

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.430
get someone else to look at it!

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.990
He didn't have to get <i>that</i> angry about it.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.140
Nogoro-kun.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.810
Why don't you just stop?

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.000
You should understand after today.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.790
With your body in the condition it's in now,
you won't be able to make it all the way to the game against Kaido.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:42.680
Actually, just a while ago, your father requested something.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.710
My dad?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.620
To not put you in any of the games.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.760
That he doesn't want to see you lose baseball again.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.270
I get it.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.620
If I pitch the way I did today,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.440
I'd just be getting in everyone's way.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.760
Oh, you can let me off here.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.470
I'll take you home.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.630
No,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.220
I just remembered I had some shopping to do.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:00.220
So all the other doctors told you no?

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:01.950
That might be so...

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.920
In the condition I'm in right now,
it's not like I can't throw a single pitch!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.980
I beg you, sensei! {sensei as in doctor... of course}

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.160
Well...

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.840
if it's only a couple of hours and you use some freezing on it, you should be all right. 

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.660
Is that true?

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.080
However,

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.270
the most I can guarantee is barely 30 pitches.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.990
If you exceed that,

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.520
forget playing in the next game, you might never be able to run at full strength again. 

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.060
I can't be held responsible for that.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.370
30 pitches, huh?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.310
Well, even so...

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.780
Also...

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.410
You're a high school student, right?

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.680
Whether it's your guardian or a family member...

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.800
if a guardian doesn't sign this permission slip,

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.310
I won't be able to inject any freezing.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.540
That's weird...

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.910
Where exactly is our stamp?

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.350
There it is!

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.190
H-Hey, what're you doing?

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.410
This is, you know...!{questionable if it's stutter.-left out on purpose -sangofe} 

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.190
What is this?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.040
This is bad.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.040
I see.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.380
So you were secretly trying to stamp the paper,

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.980
and were trying to do it without permission?

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:34.230
I-I couldn't help it.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.550
Would you have signed it if I asked you to?

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.740
That's true...

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.760
I'd have to talk to your father about it.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:42.630
Please don't.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.930
Dad's been against it since the beginning of the tournament.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.220
If you showed this to him...

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.540
Isn't it enough already?

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.440
You broke your shoulder during Little League,

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.670
so you should know very well the pain of not being able to play baseball.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.490
I heard from your father...

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:03.180
that you don't have any interest in playing as a pro,

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.120
and that you want to defeat Kaido.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:09.610
You know that your father wants you to become a pro, right?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.090
Why is it?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:17.400
Is just one game against Kaido...

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:22.090
important enough to sacrifice your entire baseball career?

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.840
It's not that, Mom.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:33.360
Yeah, at first, the goal was to defeat Kaido.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:38.010
That's why I transferred... and even built a baseball team.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:41.490
But this is... It's all <i>my</i> selfishness...

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:44.060
That's why... So that's why...

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.320
That's why... So that's why...

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.310
The baseball team that I built and got everyone involved in...

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:53.400
I can't just quit halfway through because of an injury.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:57.920
I have to take responsibility for everyone's dreams.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.910
No, not just responsibility.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:08.260
I, myself, want to fulfill the dream with those guys who stuck with someone like me.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.160
That's all it is.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.290
Take it.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.710
I'll convince your father for you.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.550
M-Mom...

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.540
Since you were little...

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.260
you weren't the kind of kid that'd listen even if we told you, right?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.800
Thanks, Mom! 

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.830
You have a game today, right?

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:04.700
Yeah.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:08.000
You're the pitcher,

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.710
so isn't it normal to wake up earlier and wake your body up?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.160
Aren't you nervous at all?

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:15.870
Of course I'm not.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.180
In the last game, no one took notice of me...

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.400
When Shigeno-senpai couldn't pitch,

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.760
the teacher and the senpai ended up relying on me.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.050
Well, of course, since you didn't produce any results.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:33.830
I'm telling you that if you're mortified about it,
start producing some results.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.520
It's because you're all talk that no one trusts you.

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:48.910
Man...

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:51.870
I'm in such a bad mood this morning...

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:52.770
Yo!

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.330
S-Senpai!

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.980
Doesn't your foot hurt?

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.040
Taiga.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.800
I have something I'd like to tell you and you alone.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.260
All right. Here I go!

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:21.760
It's like...

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:27.610
the other team's skills and the atmosphere of the game are completely different than our opponent's in the first game.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.750
Next, Seishuu High School, please begin your warmup.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.900
Well then... since I have nothing to do,

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.950
I'm going to go greet the other team.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.660
G-Greet?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.330
H-Hey!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.470
Nice pitch.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.740
You seem to be doing well, Komori.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:04.400
You too, Yamane. Seems like you're able to throw a pretty good pitch.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.730
Honda!

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:08.700
Last five pitches!

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.940
How cold!

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:16.160
Just because we're going to be battling now,
you don't have to play the bad guy.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:22.500
Isn't it rude to be coming to the opponent's bullpen?

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.860
Don't be so strict!

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:29.240
We didn't see your first game,
and you have our game on video.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:30.590
Isn't it fine if it's just for a little while?

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:34.800
What are those guys doing?

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.730
Well...

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:50.950
I had a lot of stories, but it seems the atmosphere isn't right. 

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:54.410
Today, let's both try our best.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.450
Hey, Komori.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.070
It seems as though he's injured and won't be able to play in the game today.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.340
Couldn't we have talked to him a little?

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:07.690
We can't.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.840
We can't show Honda-kun any openings.

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:16.680
Even in a game where we're 99% sure we'll win,

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:19.060
with Honda-kun as our enemy,

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.480
the slightest slip-up will be our downfall.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.380
That's why...

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.770
in order to not have any weakness in our hearts,

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.820
we have to seal away the fact that we're friends for the time being.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.040
<i>I won't lose...</i>

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.780
<i>Honda-kun.</i>

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:40.780
This is a free fansub.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:40.780
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.480
Listen up!

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.610
Today we can't rely on Shigeno!

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.250
And the opponent is a seeded school!

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:50.070
But if we show them the fighting spirit we had during the first game,

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:51.760
we have a chance as well!

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:53.870
Let's go and give it our all!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.720
YEAH!

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.490
<i>Komori and Yamane...</i>

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.060
<i>It's been two years since they joined...</i>

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.230
<i>There we go.</i>

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:16.200
<i>Coach... You're putting those up again?</i>

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.100
<i>Be quiet.</i>

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.420
<i>It's the emotion... The emotion.</i>

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:25.160
<i>The new members coming in today might become serious about it after seeing this, right?</i>

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:28.740
<i>Couldn't you at least wait until after we've won the first game?</i>

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.040
<i>That's right, that's right.</i>

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.880
<i>If you set the goal too high, it might end up making us lose our will to fight.</i>

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.310
<i>New members, line up!</i>

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.400
<i>I'm from Mifune East Junior High;</i>

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.530
<i>my name is Yamane.</i>

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:51.730
<i>I used to play third, but I broke my elbow and now I'm only able to play first.</i>

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.030
<i>M-Me too...</i>

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.710
<i>I'm from Mifune East Junior High...</i>

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:58.060
<i>What was that?</i>

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.320
<i>Talk in a louder voice.</i>

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.290
<i>M-My name is Oobayashi!</i>

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.990
<i>Um... I don't exactly have a specific position I'm good at!</i>

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:07.710
<i>All right then, next.</i>

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.390
<i>Like them, I'm from Mifune East Junior High!</i>

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:13.050
<i>I'm Komori! I was the catcher!</i>

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.050
<i>Is that so? You're very energetic.</i>

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.010
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:25.970
<i>My, my... A guy who's stuck on first, a shy tall guy,</i>

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.730
<i>and an energetic boy who seems like he belongs in Little League?</i>

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:33.900
<i>I'd like to see your skill level, so just try and catch these hard liners!</i>

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:34.950
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.030
<i>Next!</i>

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:49.510
<i>Even if he's broken his elbow, he can throw pretty well...</i>

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:50.550
<i>Next!</i>

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.550
<i>That guy...</i>

00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:59.390
<i>he's pretty good.</i>

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:06.970
<i>It's free batting, so throw with all you've got, Urasawa.</i>

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.690
<i>H-Huh?</i>

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:18.110
<i>Damn!</i>

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.850
<i>We don't need you to take it easy on us.</i>

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:34.460
<i>Because we intend to defeat Kaido... and make it to Koshien.</i>

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:38.780
<i>Y-You guys...</i>

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.170
<i>Y-You guys...</i>

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.760
<i>Last summer we were in the top 16.</i>

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.060
<i>In the Newcomers Tournament, the top eight.</i>

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:51.260
<i>We've built up our skills a little at a time.</i>

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.230
<i>Yes, Kaido is strong.</i>

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:57.480
<i>But, if it's you guys, you can do it.</i>

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.340
<i>More than anyone else or anywhere else,</i>

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:01.990
<i>if it's you guys who've sweat so much... </i>

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.120
Play ball!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.240
All right, go Taiga!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.170
Throw the first punch!

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:18.110
<i>It's not like they were seeded for nothing.</i>

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:18.900
<i>Well...</i>

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.130
<i>let's see how good they are.</i>

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:27.930
Strike!

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.900
<i>To start off, a curve...</i>

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:35.600
<i>He seems to have a lot of confidence in his control over his curve ball.</i>

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:39.510
Strike!

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.920
What're you doing, Taiga!

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.610
It's not that great of a fastball!

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.500
<i>A pitch to the low, outside corner.</i>

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.580
<i>It's a ball that you can't try and hit if you're not in trouble.</i>

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.390
Ball!

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:03.670
<i>I see; they're going to play dirty as well.</i>

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.680
Strike! Batter out!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.450
Oh my...

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:16.690
For Shimizu-kun to get three strikes all of a sudden...

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.010
Was it a breaking ball?

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.650
It was a curve that was faster than the first pitch.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:25.990
They change the speed of the curve?

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.730
For now...

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.950
that speed and ball control is extremely troublesome.

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.040
All right!

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:36.670
Out!

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.130
He hit a fly ball.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:42.530
The players that don't have the power to hit it...

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:45.090
they're allowing them to hit the ball.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.550
Batting third: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:53.560
W-What?

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:56.370
Ball.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.230
<i>T-They're walking him?</i>

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:08.240
Ball.

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:10.980
I see.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:15.470
So you won't let our only run producer swing the bat, huh?

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:16.410
Ball.

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:20.970
Ball. Four balls.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:29.130
<i>You bring me to bat, the fourth batter, and you walk him?</i>

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.600
<i>Damn. Don't mess around.</i>

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.600
Batting fourth: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.770
Do you think it's a fluke that I'm here as the fourth batter!?

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:50.110
Strike! Batter out!

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:52.120
Three outs! Change!

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.120
It's a fluke.

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:03.290
<i>So everything is going the way they calculated it?</i>

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.960
This doesn't look as though we'll be able to score a whole lot of runs.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.430
I'm counting on you, Taiga.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.230
Yeah. I'll try my best.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.810
<i>F-Freezing?</i>

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.860
<i>Yeah, just before I came here. </i>

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:23.030
<i>I had the doctor inject me.</i>

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:24.730
<i>Are you going to play in the game?</i>

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.670
<i>I haven't told the coach yet...</i>

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:29.950
<i>Also...</i>

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.740
<i>30 pitches?</i>

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.770
<i>Well, that's what the doctor says.</i>

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:41.700
<i>Don't worry about it, and just defeat everyone straight on at full strength from the beginning of the game.</i>

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:43.940
<i>If it gets hard for you,</i>

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:46.680
<i>I'll take care of the rest.</i>

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.470
<i>You got it, right, Taiga?</i>

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:54.730
<i>Without your cooperation, it's impossible for Seishuu to win and keep going!</i>

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.080
Play!

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:05.730
Strike!

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:08.060
W-What the?

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.280
This pitch is completely different from the one in the last game!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:18.790
Strike!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.500
The fastballs are better than those in their first game.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.050
Strike! Batter out!

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:31.270
All right!

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:32.260
He did it!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.480
<i>The curves are sharper too.</i>

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:40.430
<i>With this, my game calling is going to be important.</i>

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.210
All right, all right...

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:49.030
Out!

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.700
Batting third: first baseman, Oobayashi-kun.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:57.410
He's gotten better.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:06.150
All right! Look at my amazing play!

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.130
All right! Go around, go around!

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:14.750
F-Fuji-senpai...

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.300
He screwed up again.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.650
Hey... sorry...

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.270
Huh?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.270
Usually, he'd say something mean about it...

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:28.730
That idiot! He's creating unnecessary problems.

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.620
A chance to drive in a run and it's Komori, huh?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.030
This is pretty bad from the get-go.

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.270
Strike!

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:46.200
<i>The balls are faster and sharper than in the first game,</i>

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.290
<i>but the variety and patterns are according to the data.</i>

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.500
<i>It hasn't changed so much that it's troublesome.</i>

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.180
<i>Sorry, but...</i>

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:55.090
<i>I'll be taking this one!</i>

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.170
Foul!

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:04.470
So close!

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:07.440
That was dangerous...

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>He's small, but he's got power.</i>

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.940
<i>Fastballs are too dangerous.</i>

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:16.610
<i>Let's go with an outside curve that'll look like a ball.</i>

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:19.240
<i>It's fine if we give them one base.</i>

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:21.780
<i>What?</i>

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:25.610
<i>If that's the case, a fastball's fine. Just make sure that it misses!</i>

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:31.770
<i>The next one will probably be a breaking ball outside or a ball.</i>

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:33.840
<i>If it enters the strike zone, I'll get it this time!</i>

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:45.950
Out!

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:47.430
Three outs! Change!

00:22:48.770 --> 00:22:51.150
<i>A fastball... inside?</i>

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:55.400
All right!

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:56.120
Nice pitching!

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:57.850
Nice, Taiga!

00:22:57.850 --> 00:22:59.280
Nice pitching!

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:03.240
<i>That guy... He's pretty good!</i>

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:06.960
<i>He was strong-willed and knew what Komori was thinking!</i>

00:24:40.630 --> 00:24:43.180
Against Mifune, who keeps scoring runs slowly,

00:24:43.180 --> 00:24:45.210
Seishuu can't score any runs.

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:47.720
And then, Miyazaki is forced to leave midway through the game?

00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:51.730
Okay! First baseman: Shigeno Goro! It's time to make our comeback!

00:24:52.520 --> 00:24:53.770
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:55.850
Climax! The Mifune Game.

00:24:55.850 --> 00:24:58.170
Run to the stage of your dreams!
